## Why This Is Asked
Event-driven, multi-tenant systems with at-least-once delivery require robust idempotency and strict isolation. Regression must cover replay paths and cost implications under bursts.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven testing, idempotency, deduplication
- Tenant isolation and per-tenant offsets
- Replay, rollback, chaos testing, cost awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
function handleEvent(event, state){
  if (state.seen && state.seen[event.dedupId]) return state;
  state.seen = state.seen || {};
  state.seen[event.dedupId] = true;
  // process event
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate exactly-once-like semantics when a consumer crashes mid-processing?
- What metrics would you surface to detect idempotency drift across tenants?

